Editorial                     NannyMUD Times                     Page 2

  Welcome to the October issue of the NannyMUD Times.
  
  I would like to thank everyone for all the positive feedback that I've
  received for starting up the printing presses again. I would also like
  to thank all the people that have contributed to this issues.

  The sudoku section of the paper has been discontinued due to lack of
  interest, or maybe it was too hard. For all the sudoku fans out there,
  Vulcan's sudoku puzzles can still be found in Xonder's House of Games.
  
  The Times is always looking for reporters. You can submit articles
  at the newspaper stand or mail them directly to me. I am currently
  looking for people to write reviews of clubs, pubs, areas, and quests.
  As you will see in the puzzles page, a couple of the puzzles this
  month were submitted by players, so if you have a good puzzles send
  it in. I am also looking for someone to write a NannyMUD quiz.
  If your interested in contributing, let me know. 
  
  You can also submit advertisements, personal ads, announcements, 
  and comics/jokes at the newspaper stand as well. There is also a 
  new section in the paper for player submitted questions and answers, 
  see page 14 in this paper for this months question, or read the 
  notice at the newspaper stand for more details.

  -Astrodeath
  
